WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:05.960
KATIE OSBERG: Hi, there.

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:08.530
My name's Katie Osberg, And I
link global retail partnerships

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.230
for Google's new and exciting
suite of business communication

00:00:11.230 --> 00:00:12.400
products.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.650
Today, my colleague Sean and
I cannot be more thrilled

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.860
to share our most recent launch,
Google Business Messages.

00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:19.750
But before we dive into
what our product is,

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.360
or even how it works, it's
helpful to understand why

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:25.110
this technology is so critical.

00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:27.170
As with all great
tech evolutions,

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:29.340
the solution often
stems from a problem,

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.390
and ours is no different.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:33.000
So, briefly, I'm
going to ask you

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.100
to put your user
hat on for a moment

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.802
and humor me as I
pose a few questions.

00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:39.510
How many of you have
experienced at least

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:42.390
one or more the
following situations

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.740
over the last couple of months?

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.150
Might you have had
to rebook travel?

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.650
Perhaps you remember the feeling
of going to multiple stores

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:53.392
and still not finding the
product you were looking for.

00:00:53.392 --> 00:00:55.350
Or could it be that you
were working from home,

00:00:55.350 --> 00:00:56.850
or perhaps your
kids were completing

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.550
their e-learning course,
and suddenly your internet

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:01.020
went out?

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.030
In all of those
situations, users

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:05.860
needed to get in touch
with brands or businesses.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.830
But because there was
an outreach spike,

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.920
these critical connections
were seemingly impossible.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.930
Almost every business
was promoting

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:15.110
on either their website
or answering machine

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.250
that call volumes
were up and wait times

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.230
were exceptionally long.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.570
Few provided alternative
means to get in touch,

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.270
and resolution-- at least in
a manner that was convenient--

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.220
say, on the user's terms--

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.170
seemed impossible.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:31.860
Now, if I am the customer, when
I hear "exceptionally long wait

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.690
times," I think, great.

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.430
This is going to take forever.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:37.830
And who has the time to
wait on hold anymore?

00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:41.220
Time and attention has become
increasingly more valuable.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.750
And while exacerbated
by the global pandemic,

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.230
this concept is not new.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:49.330
Users are just simply pulled
in too many directions.

00:01:49.330 --> 00:01:51.697
But the same can be
said for businesses now.

00:01:51.697 --> 00:01:53.280
In addition to the
overwhelming demand

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:56.260
to speak to someone caused
by the global pandemic,

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:58.200
it's no secret that
businesses have also

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.360
been tasked with an influx
of new responsibilities.

00:02:01.360 --> 00:02:03.780
For example, most are
instituting new health

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.760
standards to keep
employees safe,

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:08.009
and many are adjusting
their operational protocols

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:12.150
to meet new and evolving
consumption behaviors.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.745
Absent of user demands to
diversify interaction channels,

00:02:15.745 --> 00:02:17.370
businesses are going
to have to rethink

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.430
the way they communicate
with customers, such

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:21.660
that interactions
are more meaningful,

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.660
result in resolutions,
and ultimately drive

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.020
connections that count.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.990
Now, we at Google
understand that we're

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.720
often responsible for
facilitating that connection

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.190
between a user and a brand.

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:35.920
And over the last
20 years, we've

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.630
worked to perfect
the art of surfacing

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.260
the right product, service, and
business in the moments that

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:42.510
matter.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:44.570
But as technology
evolves, we've come

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:46.430
to understand that
surfacing a call button--

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:48.722
or perhaps a link to
a Contact Us page--

00:02:48.722 --> 00:02:50.180
might not be the
most effective way

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:52.950
for us to facilitate
this connection.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.740
In fact, these
connections can be

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.390
incredibly expensive
for businesses

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.565
and extremely
frustrating for users.

00:02:58.565 --> 00:03:01.760
Did you know that businesses
spend $1.3 trillion

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.570
on 265 billion customer
service calls each year?

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:08.970
And 67% of people
raised their hand

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.400
indicating that they would
rather message a business

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.470
than speak with a person.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.360
The communication
experiences of today

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.160
are expensive, frustrating,
and frankly inconvenient.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.760
Which is why users have begun to
demand conversational messaging

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.480
solutions, not just from Google,
but from their favorite brands

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.190
and businesses.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.375
To be successful in this space,
it has become abundantly clear

00:03:32.375 --> 00:03:34.500
that three things must be
true about your messaging

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:36.390
experiences.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:39.000
They must be asynchronous,
enabling users

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:41.160
to pick up and exit
the conversation

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:43.050
at their convenience.

00:03:43.050 --> 00:03:47.270
Automated, returning responses
to users in real time.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:50.190
And finally, assisted,
helping users

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:54.020
to determine which products or
services are right for them.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.670
Today, as a result
of these learnings,

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.410
we couldn't be more
excited to share

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.290
how we've evolved the Google
search experience to facilitate

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.180
making connections that count.

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:03.080
Over to you, Sean.

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.290
SEAN FALCONER: Thanks, Katie.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:09.180
My name is Sean
Falconer, and I lead

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.700
developer relations for
Google's business communication

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:12.790
products.

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.970
And I'm going to take you
through our conversational

00:04:14.970 --> 00:04:17.110
solution, Business Messages.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.970
So, what exactly is
Business Messages?

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:22.670
Business Messages lets
your customers message

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:26.330
your business directly from
your Search and Maps results.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:29.090
As Katie described, many
business conversations

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:32.007
begin on a Google surface
like Search or Maps.

00:04:32.007 --> 00:04:33.590
And until recently,
customers are both

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:35.737
calling your business
for support or digging

00:04:35.737 --> 00:04:38.320
through your website to find the
correct means to contact you.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.170
With Business Messages,
you can provide customers

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:46.770
high-quality help through
your Search and Maps results.

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.140
Instead of the customer being
redirected to your phone system

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.032
or website, they will
see a message button

00:04:52.032 --> 00:04:53.490
where they can
begin a conversation

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.282
with your business.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:59.240
So, how do you go about creating
a conversational experience

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:01.640
for your business with
Business Messages?

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.700
Let's take a look.

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.740
As a consumer, your
customer user journey

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.540
begins as it does today, by
searching for that business

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:11.120
on Google Search.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:13.460
Once you find the business
you're trying to contact,

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:16.070
instead of only seeing Call,
Directions, and Website

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:20.180
buttons, business enabled with
Business Messages will also

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:21.710
have a Message button.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.300
Tapping on the
message button will

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.580
launch a conversational
surface where you can begin

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:27.470
chatting with that business.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.030
These conversations can begin
on an iOS or Android device.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:35.630
Behind the scenes,
what is happening is

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:38.570
the messages sent from consumers
are passed through the Business

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.790
Messages API through
to a messaging

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:42.620
partner or your
business directly

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:44.750
via a configured webhook.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.840
Once you receive the message,
you can pass that message

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:49.160
to a live or digital agent.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:54.810
This diagram shows this process
in a little more detail.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:57.920
The user or consumer
begins on Search or Maps,

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:59.990
looks up a business,
opens a conversation

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.880
with that business,
is greeted with

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:05.360
a customized welcome message,
and begins a conversation.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:07.520
Messages from the
consumer are passed

00:06:07.520 --> 00:06:10.100
through the northbound
API and push your webhook

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.240
as a JSON object.

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.970
The webhook parses
the received object

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:16.490
that contains the consumer's
message, the preferred

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:18.755
language of the user,
timestamp information,

00:06:18.755 --> 00:06:22.940
a unique conversation ID, and
the consumer's display name.

00:06:22.940 --> 00:06:25.030
Within your webhook, you
can route that message

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.040
to a digital agent as
your first line of defense

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.750
for handling common
customer support issues,

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.030
or pass the conversation
over to a live agent

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.940
to handle more
complex user journeys.

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:39.800
Business Messages helps you
leverage the existing user

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:41.800
behavior to contact your
business through Search

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:44.380
or Maps, where you can
continue to take advantage

00:06:44.380 --> 00:06:46.660
of the discovery and
reach of these products,

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:48.700
while providing
a more direct way

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:51.340
for you to have real and
meaningful personalized

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:55.340
conversations with
your consumers.

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:57.550
The Business Messages
platform and API sports

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.610
which features like cards,
carousels, suggestion chips,

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:03.040
photos, and actions
that help you deep

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.020
link into your website or app.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.850
By utilizing these
rich features,

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:09.070
you can create an
engaging user journey

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:12.200
to capture leads, sell products,
or solve customer support

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:12.700
issues.

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:17.730
By combining the
discovery and reach

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.790
of your business on Search,
along with the rich features I

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:24.090
just mentioned, and automation
through a digital agent,

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.400
you can help your consumers
solve customer issues

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:29.190
without the cost of a
phone call or live agent.

00:07:29.190 --> 00:07:32.010
Like with an app or website,
the Business Messages'

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:34.230
rich features help
you direct the user

00:07:34.230 --> 00:07:37.560
through a supported user journey
that can be fully automated.

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:40.020
Digital agents can be
created using tools

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:43.410
like Google Cloud's Dialogflow,
our tool for creating

00:07:43.410 --> 00:07:46.400
agents that understand
natural language.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:48.440
Companies like Walmart
have these Dialogflow

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:51.510
to not only power their digital
agent on Business Messages,

00:07:51.510 --> 00:07:53.810
but also automate a large
majority of customer support

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.660
inquiries, leaving
their life agents

00:07:55.660 --> 00:08:01.050
available to handle a more
complex and unique requests.

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:03.160
Business Messages
is an innovation

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:05.345
in creating true
customer connections.

00:08:05.345 --> 00:08:06.720
The rich features
of the platform

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:09.460
help you put guardrails around
your automated experiences

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.640
so you can steer your
consumers through a happy path

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.270
to solve problems.

00:08:14.270 --> 00:08:16.210
But aside of the
fancy features, this

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:17.710
is a conversational platform.

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:20.890
Your customer is conversing
directly with your business.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.960
Utilizing tools
like Dialogflow help

00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.710
you to automatically respond
quickly and naturally

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.080
to customers, regardless
of the time of day,

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.340
or current mode on
your live agents.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.299
The combination of a natural
entry point from Search,

00:08:33.299 --> 00:08:36.640
the rich user interface, and
the powerful automation provided

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:38.740
by tools like
Dialogflow represent

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:43.110
a true technological innovation.

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:45.200
In fact, we see
these major shifts

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:47.580
in how consumers interact
with technology and businesses

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.820
every 10 years or so.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.920
Back in the '70s,
we had mainframes.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.570
In the '80s, we had
desktop computing.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:56.600
In the mid-'90s, the internet,
and then in the mid aughts,

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.820
mobile and smartphone
revolution.

00:08:58.820 --> 00:09:02.570
It's now hard to imagine a world
today without a smartphone.

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:05.405
We're all walking around with
a small computer in our pocket.

00:09:05.405 --> 00:09:07.280
This would have been
unheard of 20 years ago,

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.560
but it completely changed
how your consumers interact

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.030
with their business.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.790
You had to adapt to creating
an app for your business,

00:09:13.790 --> 00:09:15.320
redesigning your
website to adapt

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.430
to smartphone screen sizes.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:19.750
And now, I believe the
next shift that's happening

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:21.900
is around AI messaging
and personalized

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.870
rich conversations.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:25.860
Business Messages
is Google's solution

00:09:25.860 --> 00:09:31.420
to help your business adapt to
this technological evolution.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:31.920
All right.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.003
Let's take a look at a
couple real world examples.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.510
This first demo is
from Walmart, who's

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:40.130
live with Business
Messages for some

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:42.600
of their locations
in the United States.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.420
They deployed a digital
agent for experience,

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:48.060
where they use Dialogflow to
create a conversational agent

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.430
that can address common
customer support issues,

00:09:50.430 --> 00:09:53.700
like opening senior
hours, COVID-19 protocols,

00:09:53.700 --> 00:09:55.880
and looking up store locations.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.540
Their Business
Messages webhook is

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:00.270
using Node.js to call
in Dialogflow APIs

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:02.410
to power the digital agent.

00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.470
They did a lot of
iteration on automation,

00:10:04.470 --> 00:10:06.660
reviewing where the
original Dialogflow

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.152
agent was unable to help, and
made iterative improvements.

00:10:10.152 --> 00:10:12.360
They're now handling the
majority of customer support

00:10:12.360 --> 00:10:14.580
requests through
their automation.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:17.163
Let's take a look
at their experience.

00:10:17.163 --> 00:10:19.830
Let's begin our journey to speak
to my local Walmart, the Google

00:10:19.830 --> 00:10:20.990
Search.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:22.700
So, I look up Walmart
San Jose, and I'm

00:10:22.700 --> 00:10:24.840
shown a few different
potential locations.

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:26.940
I choose the Walmart
Supercenter that I know,

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:29.520
and I see the local
listing result.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:31.380
To begin my chat
experience, I tap

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:34.140
on Message, which opens
a conversational overlay

00:10:34.140 --> 00:10:36.150
with this specific Walmart.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:37.920
I see a customized
welcome message,

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:40.200
letting me know what this
chat bot can help me with.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:42.740
I choose to agree to
continue my conversation.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:44.850
Once the chat bot receives
my acknowledgment,

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:46.890
my conversation with the
digital agent begins.

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:49.065
From the greeting, I
can see a chip list

00:10:49.065 --> 00:10:52.620
of the various types of user
journeys the chat bot supports.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:55.640
Things like hiring, pickup
times, inventory, hours,

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:58.270
store safety, and so on.

00:10:58.270 --> 00:11:01.320
There's really a lot that the
chat bot can help me with.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.500
I'm going to choose store hours.

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:05.270
When I choose this
item, the request

00:11:05.270 --> 00:11:08.300
is being sent back through
the Business Messages API

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.520
to the Walmart webhook,
and then the webhook

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:12.560
is sending this
request to Dialogflow

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:15.810
to compute a response based on
the query, and in this case,

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:18.760
the specific Walmart
location that I asked about.

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:20.580
Because this is
a chat interface,

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:22.130
I can also just type my request.

00:11:22.130 --> 00:11:25.100
So I'm going to ask, do
I have to wear a mask?

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:26.620
Once I hit send,
the same process

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.870
to handle this message through
Walmart's digital agent

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.170
will be carried out.

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:32.030
And we can see that
since July 20th,

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:33.720
all shoppers have
to wear a mask.

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:35.860
This is super helpful.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:37.830
I'm going to ask
one more question.

